<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115057" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρωμᾰτ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of, relating to colour</i>:—but only found,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph., in Rhet.,
				<i>offering a colourable pretext</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρῶμα</span> IV.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ χ.,</span> as name of a form
			of rebuttal, Aps.<i><span class="en">
				p.273H.
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρωμάτιον</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Music,
				<i>chromatic</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρῶμα</span>
			IV. <i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελῳδία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Comp.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλος,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάτονον, ἐναρμόνιον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.18
			</span></i>, cf. Aristox(?).<i><span class="en">
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				667.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κὸν [γένος</span>] the
				<i>chromatic genus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.744c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.63K.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.321
			</span></i>.</div>
